"Pass extracted TLD to CompactEncDet::DetectEncoding()" (crbug 578671521;
no CVE listed yet): text encoding detection took its TLD hint from the full
URL, and a colon in the userinfo ("http://a.jp:x@example.com/") let a page
spoof it, steering the detected charset. chromium/src main commit
3d786246808bf5db19af9953395db3ceaad62a71, merged on 2026-10-30 to 158 and
to 157 as ceee4f5c20ca0cd40531ecd140b9ec16375ee0ff
(refs/branch-heads/8103@{#991}, after the 157.0.8103.33 tag). This is the
157 merge, without its test; it adds a kill switch,
TextEncodingDetectorTldHint (enabled). Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

